### My final recommendation

There is one thing I particularly want you to avoid: allowing Google AI Studio to make AutoTech look finished while leaving its electrical calculations inaccurate.

A good-looking automotive simulator is easy to generate. A simulator that correctly calculates voltage, resistance, current, sensor outputs, fault conditions, and waveforms is considerably harder.

Prioritize mathematical accuracy, then instrument integration, then AI features and visual polish.

